-  sept [order=10]
-  shrine_types [order=20]
-  lain [order=30]
'  chore: the general async-task driver vocabulary.  A chore is a
'  computation run off the coordinator's event loop: a request record
'  MADE under a chore driver's /io name selects a boot-registered
'  family by iota; the host worker plans jobs, runs each in a leaf
'  actor, writes the family's results back through the cmd vocabulary
'  below, and pokes a completion record onto the request node.
+  chore
  +  req
    '  A chore request as a namespace record: just the family
    '  selector.  Families layer their own argument slots on top.
    \  fam=iota
    ^  myth
    =  t  myth/new
    t.put(['fam] (pails/q fam))
  +  cfg
    '  The record for a chore driver node: the shared driver inbox
    '  kook, plus the family requests default to when they carry no
    '  ['fam] of their own.
    \  fam=iota
    ^  myth
    =  t1  (kooked [['kook 'dtake]])
    t1.put(['fam] (pails/q fam))
  +  fam_of
    '  A record's family: its own ['fam], else the default.
    \  dflt=iota t=myth
    ^  iota
    ?  t.quip_at(['fam])
     > (./some q=iota)  q
     > .none  dflt
  +  done_t
    '  The request node's completion record.
    \  passed=nat failed=nat
    ^  myth
    =  t1  myth/new
    =  t2  t1.put(['res_done] (pd 1))
    =  t3  t2.put(['passed] (pd passed))
    t3.put(['failed] (pd failed))
  +  fail_t
    '  The completion record for a request the driver could not run
    '  (unknown family, plan failure).
    \  e=iota
    ^  myth
    =  t1  myth/new
    =  t2  t1.put(['res_done] (pd 1))
    =  t3  t2.put(['res_ok] (pd 0))
    t3.put(['res_err] (pails/q e))
  +  clear_t
    '  The driver-record poke clearing a request kid's fresh marker.
    \  kid=iota
    ^  myth
    =  t  myth/new
    t.put(['fresh kid] (pd 0))
  +  cmd
    '  The write vocabulary a finished job returns: what the driver
    '  should write where.  mkp is a make retried as a poke when the
    '  node already exists — the verdict-child idiom.
    &  chore/cmd/mkp
       chore/cmd/make
       chore/cmd/poke

    +  mkp
      :  pax=path t=myth

    +  make
      :  pax=path t=myth

    +  poke
      :  pax=path t=myth

  +  mkp_t
    '  Constructor laws for hosts: a sum member's own entry is not
    '  callable across the FFI, so cmd values are minted here.
    \  pax=path t=myth
    ^  chore/cmd
    (./mkp pax t)
  +  make_t
    \  pax=path t=myth
    ^  chore/cmd
    (./make pax t)
  +  poke_t
    \  pax=path t=myth
    ^  chore/cmd
    (./poke pax t)
  +  cmd_parts
    '  A cmd's write, host-shaped: kind 0 mkp, 1 make, 2 poke — hosts
    '  read the anonymous row positionally instead of guessing at
    '  nominal reps.
    \  c=chore/cmd
    ^  [k=nat pax=path t=myth]
    ?  c
     > (./mkp pax t)  [0 pax t]
     > (./make pax2 t2)  [1 pax2 t2]
     > (./poke pax3 t3)  [2 pax3 t3]
